An anonymous block (an inline `[%css]` with no binding) writes `:focus`
then `:hover`. The two named blocks `hover` and `focus` define the same two
atoms earlier, in the opposite order, so definition order alone puts
`:hover` first and `:focus` wins when both apply. The anonymous block is not
in `[@@@css.bindings]`; the ppx lists it in `[@@@css.blocks]` (line
of the CSS string, classes in source order) next to the named blocks:

  $ refmt --parse re --print ml input.re > input.ml

  $ ../../standalone.exe --impl input.ml -o output.ml
  $ cat output.ml
  [@@@css "._a_qyw7u4ego80:hover{color:red;}"]
  [@@@css "._a_0lub34ebzcl:focus{color:blue;}"]
  [@@@css.bindings
    [("Input.hover", "_id_15yirr8", "_a_qyw7u4ego80");
    ("Input.focus", "_id_npabso", "_a_0lub34ebzcl")]]
  [@@@css.blocks
    [(1, "_id_15yirr8 _a_qyw7u4ego80");
    (2, "_id_npabso _a_0lub34ebzcl");
    (5, "_a_0lub34ebzcl _a_qyw7u4ego80")]]
  let hover = CSS.make "label:hover _id_15yirr8 _a_qyw7u4ego80" []
  let focus = CSS.make "label:focus _id_npabso _a_0lub34ebzcl" []
  let _ = CSS.className (CSS.make "_a_0lub34ebzcl _a_qyw7u4ego80" [])
  let _ = (hover, focus)

With the payload, generate adds the block edge "focus before hover", and
`:hover`, written last in the anonymous block, wins:

  $ styled-ppx.generate output.ml
  /* This file is generated by styled-ppx, do not edit manually */
  ._a_0lub34ebzcl:focus{color:blue;}
  ._a_qyw7u4ego80:hover{color:red;}

Without the `[@@@css.blocks]` line, the anonymous block's edge is lost and
definition order puts `:focus` last:

  $ sed '/css.blocks/,/)]]$/d' output.ml > no_blocks.ml
  $ styled-ppx.generate no_blocks.ml
  /* This file is generated by styled-ppx, do not edit manually */
  ._a_qyw7u4ego80:hover{color:red;}
  ._a_0lub34ebzcl:focus{color:blue;}
